onsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5a75df98ecfb5da5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLooking at state/jurisdiction performance for eighth-graders in public schools, average scores were lower in 51 states/jurisdictions and not significantly different in 2. This is the largest number of states/jurisdictions with score declines in grade 8 mathematics going back to 2003. Among the states/jurisdictions with score declines, 18 scored lower than the national average score for public school students in 2022; 16 had average scores that were not significantly different from the national public average; and 17 scored higher. Explore detailed state average score results in the NAEP Mathematics Report Card\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5a75df98ecfb5da5\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "NAEP 2022 grade 8 mathematics average score Arizona 270", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 1089, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6cd34d60ab693276\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6cd34d60ab693276\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b5cb2a7dbfd82252\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b5cb2a7dbfd82252\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"911eb8aef63090c4\">>>\nSource: 