ool students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7ad6e7279b5c9ba3\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"07b3a9ec7f94f1eb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNational, South Carolina 2022 NAEP Results Released - South Carolina Department of Education - 05/17/2025 7:37 PM\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"07b3a9ec7f94f1eb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ed.sc.gov/newsroom/news-releases/national-south-carolina-2022-naep-results-released/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2c671948a1b01200\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRequired by federal law, NAEP is administered to samples of students in each state and provides a means for valid nationwide comparisons of academic achievement. Approximately 3,700 fourth-graders and 3,600 eighth-graders participated from South Carolina. Scores on the NAEP reading and mathematics tests are reported on a 500-point scale and as percentages in achievement levels: Below NAEP Basic, NAEP Basic, NAEP Proficient, and NAEP Advanced.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2c671948a1b01200\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 24, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ed.sc.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d5de2ec64a920cbd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 Mathematics Snapshot Report: South Carolina Grade 8\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d5de2ec64a920cbd\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011SC8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0a1a9346d94e9ec3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0a1a9346d94e9ec3\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\